 "_note": "Official miHoYo 2.8_live hotpatch outputs (the final in-version state a 2022 client ended with). Same mechanism as 1.6: the agent mirrors these files -- first as one ready-made bundle from archive.org (`bundles`, resumable, md5 + size pinned), then file by file from the official CDN (`upstreams`) for whatever is still missing, or entirely when the bundle cannot be used -- verifies them against the md5/size below (copied from the official index files), serves them token-less under /hotpatch/<path> and makes the dispatch advertise them. Payloads = every file that differs from the shipped 2.8.0 client (GenshinImpact_2.8.0.zip, res_revision 8078355 / data_revision 8078038 / silence_revision 8017153) plus the complete silence set; see docs/HOTFIX-1.6.md section 6.",
 "upstreams": [
  "https://autopatchhk.yuanshen.com",
  "https://autopatchcn.yuanshen.com"
 ],
 "_bundleNote": "Ready-made bundles of the same files on archive.org (CDN-relative layout inside: client_game_res/... and client_design_data/...; a voice bundle holds client_game_res/<branch>/<res.base output>/client/StandaloneWindows64/AudioAssets/<Lang>/*.pck). The agent downloads a bundle first (resumable, md5 + size verified), unpacks it into a staging folder OUTSIDE the mirror and moves ONLY the files whose md5/size match this manifest (or, for voice packs, the mirrored official release index) into the mirror; whatever is still missing comes from `upstreams` file by file, which is also the whole path when a bundle cannot be used (no 7z tool, less than half the bytes missing, not enough disk, download failure). url is stored percent-encoded and used as-is; md5/size = the values of the archive.org item's <item>_files.xml. GIO_HOTPATCH_BUNDLES=0 switches the bundles off.",
